{"id":"63d29d1fbf07993375698df340445199ad2aaf9e","axis":"silent","repo":"quarkusio/quarkus","sha":"63d29d1fbf07993375698df340445199ad2aaf9e","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"core/deployment/src/main/java/io/quarkus/deployment/Capability.java","lines":["@@ -128,6 +128,8 @@ public interface Capability {","     String OPENTELEMETRY_METRICS = QUARKUS_PREFIX + \".opentelemetry.metrics\";","     String OPENTELEMETRY_LOGS = QUARKUS_PREFIX + \".opentelemetry.logs\";"," ","+    String MICROMETER_OPENTELEMETRY = QUARKUS_PREFIX + \".micrometer.opentelemetry\";","+","     String OPENSHIFT = QUARKUS_PREFIX + \".openshift\";","     String OPENSHIFT_CLIENT = OPENSHIFT + \".client\";"," "],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/src/main/asciidoc/opentelemetry-metrics.adoc","lines":["@@ -704,6 +704,29 @@ The native image assessment above was performed using GraalVM 23.0.2."," The Micrometer to OpenTelemetry bridge unifies all telemetry in Quarkus. It generates Micrometer's metrics but sends"," them along the OpenTelemetry telemetry output. For more details please visit the xref:telemetry-micrometer-to-opentelemetry.adoc[Micrometer and OpenTelemetry extension]."," ","+[[redundant-metrics-warning]]","+=== Avoiding redundant metrics collection","+","+Collecting metrics with both a Micrometer registry (such as `quarkus-micrometer-registry-prometheus`) and OpenTelemetry metrics at the same time is redundant: the measurements are gathered and exported by two independent pipelines, adding memory and runtime overhead.","+","+To help detect this, Quarkus logs a build-time warning when a Micrometer metrics registry is present together with OpenTelemetry metrics, unless you are using the `quarkus-micrometer-opentelemetry` extension:","+","+[source,text]","+----","+Redundant metrics collection detected: both Micrometer (registries: %s) and OpenTelemetry are active. Consider disabling one system (e.g., setting quarkus.otel.metrics.enabled=false).","+----","+","+To resolve the warning, choose one of the following:","+","+- Use the xref:telemetry-micrometer-to-opentelemetry.adoc[`quarkus-micrometer-opentelemetry`] extension, which lets Micrometer metrics flow through the OpenTelemetry SDK with a single pipeline.","+- Keep OpenTelemetry metrics and remove the Micrometer registry.","+- Keep the Micrometer registry (for example, when OpenTelemetry is used only for tracing) and disable OpenTelemetry metrics:","++","+[source,properties]","+----","+quarkus.otel.metrics.enabled=false","+----","+"," == Exporters"," See the main xref:opentelemetry.adoc#exporters[OpenTelemetry Guide exporters] section."," "],"additions":23,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/src/main/asciidoc/telemetry-micrometer-to-opentelemetry.adoc","lines":["@@ -41,6 +41,12 @@ The output telemetry data is handled by the OpenTelemetry SDK and sent by the `q"," "," This reduces the overhead of having an independent Micrometer registry plus the OpenTelemetry SDK in memory for the same application when both `quarkus-micrometer` and `quarkus-opentelemetry` extensions are used independently."," ","+[NOTE]","+====","+Using a Micrometer registry (such as `quarkus-micrometer-registry-prometheus`) together with OpenTelemetry metrics collects the same measurements twice. Quarkus logs a build-time warning in that case.","+See xref:opentelemetry-metrics.adoc#redundant-metrics-warning[Avoiding redundant metrics collection] for the available options, including this extension.","+====","+"," *The OpenTelemetry SDK will handle all metrics.* Either Micrometer metrics (manual or automatic) and OpenTelemetry Metrics can be used. All are available with this single extension."," "," All the configurations from the OpenTelemetry and Micrometer extensions are available with `quarkus-micrometer-opentelemetry`."],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/micrometer-opentelemetry/deployment/src/test/java/io/quarkus/micrometer/opentelemetry/deployment/RedundantMetricsBridgeNoWarningTest.java","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@","+package io.quarkus.micrometer.opentelemetry.deployment;","+","+import static org.assertj.core.api.Assertions.assertThat;","+","+import java.util.function.Consumer;","+import java.util.logging.Level;","+import java.util.logging.LogRecord;","+","+import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;","+import org.junit.jupiter.api.extension.RegisterExtension;","+","+import io.micrometer.core.instrument.simple.SimpleMeterRegistry;","+import io.quarkus.builder.BuildChainBuilder;","+import io.quarkus.builder.BuildContext;","+import io.quarkus.builder.BuildStep;","+import io.quarkus.micrometer.deployment.MicrometerProcessor;","+import io.quarkus.micrometer.deployment.MicrometerRegistryProviderBuildItem;","+import io.quarkus.test.QuarkusExtensionTest;","+","+class RedundantMetricsBridgeNoWarningTest {","+","+    @SuppressWarnings(\"Convert2Lambda\")","+    @RegisterExtension","+    static final QuarkusExtensionTest config = new QuarkusExtensionTest()","+            .overrideConfigKey(\"quarkus.otel.metrics.enabled\", \"true\")","+            .overrideConfigKey(\"quarkus.otel.exporter.otlp.enabled\", \"false\")","+            .overrideConfigKey(\"quarkus.devservices.enabled\", \"false\")","+            // Disable the OTel metrics to ensure we don't get a warning","+            .overrideConfigKey(\"quarkus.otel.metrics.enabled\", \"false\")","+            // Stand in for a third-party registry that only produces the SPI build item.","+            .addBuildChainCustomizer(new Consumer<>() {","+                @Override","+                public void accept(BuildChainBuilder builder) {","+                    builder.addBuildStep(new BuildStep() {","+                        @Override","+                        public void execute(BuildContext context) {","+                            context.produce(new MicrometerRegistryProviderBuildItem(SimpleMeterRegistry.class));","+                        }","+                    }).produces(MicrometerRegistryProviderBuildItem.class).build();","+                }","+            })","+            .withEmptyApplication()","+            .setLogRecordPredicate(record -> record.getLevel().intValue() >= Level.WARNING.intValue()","+                    && MicrometerProcessor.class.getName().equals(record.getLoggerName()))","+            .assertLogRecords(records -> assertThat(records)","+                    .extracting(LogRecord::getMessage)","+                    .isEmpty());","+","+    @Test","+    void otelDisabledNoWarning() {","+    }","+}"],"additions":52,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/micrometer-opentelemetry/deployment/src/test/java/io/quarkus/micrometer/opentelemetry/deployment/RedundantMetricsBridgeWarningTest.java","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@","+package io.quarkus.micrometer.opentelemetry.deployment;","+","+import static org.assertj.core.api.Assertions.assertThat;","+","+import java.util.function.Consumer;","+import java.util.logging.Level;","+","+import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;","+import org.junit.jupiter.api.extension.RegisterExtension;","+","+import io.micrometer.core.instrument.simple.SimpleMeterRegistry;","+import io.quarkus.builder.BuildChainBuilder;","+import io.quarkus.builder.BuildContext;","+import io.quarkus.builder.BuildStep;","+import io.quarkus.micrometer.deployment.MicrometerProcessor;","+import io.quarkus.micrometer.deployment.MicrometerRegistryProviderBuildItem;","+import io.quarkus.test.QuarkusExtensionTest;","+","+class RedundantMetricsBridgeWarningTest {","+","+    @SuppressWarnings(\"Convert2Lambda\")","+    @RegisterExtension","+    static final QuarkusExtensionTest config = new QuarkusExtensionTest()","+            .overrideConfigKey(\"quarkus.otel.metrics.enabled\", \"true\")","+            .overrideConfigKey(\"quarkus.otel.exporter.otlp.enabled\", \"false\")","+            .overrideConfigKey(\"quarkus.devservices.enabled\", \"false\")","+            // Stand in for a third-party registry that only produces the SPI build item.","+            .addBuildChainCustomizer(new Consumer<>() {","+                @Override","+                public void accept(BuildChainBuilder builder) {","+                    builder.addBuildStep(new BuildStep() {","+                        @Override","+                        public void execute(BuildContext context) {","+                            context.produce(new MicrometerRegistryProviderBuildItem(SimpleMeterRegistry.class));","+                        }","+                    }).produces(MicrometerRegistryProviderBuildItem.class).build();","+                }","+            })","+            .withEmptyApplication()","+            .setLogRecordPredicate(record -> record.getLevel().intValue() >= Level.WARNING.intValue()","+                    && MicrometerProcessor.class.getName().equals(record.getLoggerName()))","+            .assertLogRecords(records -> assertThat(records)","+                    .hasSize(1)","+                    .allSatisfy(record -> assertThat(record.getMessage())","+                            .startsWith(\"Redundant\")","+                            .contains(\"Micrometer (registries:\", \"and OpenTelemetry\")));","+","+    @Test","+    void warnsForAnyRegistryProvider() {","+    }","+}"],"additions":51,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/micrometer-opentelemetry/runtime/pom.xml","lines":["@@ -53,6 +53,11 @@","             <plugin>","                 <groupId>io.quarkus</groupId>","                 <artifactId>quarkus-extension-maven-plugin</artifactId>","+                <configuration>","+                    <capabilities>","+                        <provides>io.quarkus.micrometer.opentelemetry</provides>","+                    </capabilities>","+                </configuration>","             </plugin>","             <plugin>","                 <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/micrometer/deployment/src/main/java/io/quarkus/